<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Church of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1534">1534</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Anglican Church</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> is the established Christian church of England, which broke from papal authority under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> in 1534 and took a Protestant form under Edward VI and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>, with the monarch as supreme governor. It was established by law in several English colonies, and dissenters such as the Pilgrims of Plymouth left it to worship separately.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/church-of-england.jpg" alt="Church of England" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Church of England · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_Church_of_England.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
